    },
    "body": "ARM64 CCMP/CCMN register and immediate instructions now execute as generated x86 operations in 32-bit and 64-bit forms. Conditions use committed guest NZCV, including the A64 always-true AL/NV predicates; false conditions replace NZCV with the encoded fallback. General registers, SP, other PSTATE bits and existing memory/MMU boundaries are preserved.\n\nThe condition emitter is shared with existing conditional branches. The complete native regression suite, 34,264 conditional cases with 137,070 assertions, 93 architectural reference tests, 12 actual C-to-Rust provider cases and an independent 3,668-case Arm oracle pass in a fresh standalone clone. Deliberate NV and flag corruption controls fail as expected. The module CI now runs the independent oracle. Existing scalar/pair/MMU/PAC regressions also pass.\n\nThis extends the instruction set only. Native translated memory, normal macOS boot and guest Metal remain separate incomplete work.",
